The primary use almost implies introducting buried random items to the
game, which would be easily ignored without using such a detector or
the various item detection one-time-use items.  It might be useful
with my own (neglected) Terrain/Island patch, since it has buried
items, but there's already a hint about their existance.  If these
items are always in chests, and if chests are all considered to have
metal components, then metal detectors become very useful indeed,
especially considering the items that chests tend to get generated
with.

Using it for finding bear traps and land mines is potentially very
helpful, since it gives players a method of building up a supply of
these without searching every step (or having automatic searching). 
And I've already mentioned it'd help players not pick up lodestones if
it's in a corner or they don't know about kicking.


